  - m_Id: 100000000022
    m_Localized: 
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000023
    m_Localized: "Madame Quacking!\nI cannot express in words how grateful I am for
      your reception. As a man of science, I had hoped until the last that I could
      manage without\u2026esoteric indulgences, yet the police are powerless. I beg
      you, madame, look \nnto the past and tell me\nwho killed my wife!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000024
    m_Localized: "It was a gloomy evening.\nFoxicia and I set forth by carriage for
      the estate of Sir Oswald Blackmore \u2014 the wealthiest badger in the kingdom.
      He was hosting a charity dinner, at which Foxicia was to perform."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000025
    m_Localized: 'The reception was splendid, and the guests numerous. Yet Foxicia

      and
      I spent the first part of the evening apart.

      Many approached her, as
      one would a celebrated pianist. I, meanwhile, encountered Lady Bella Nottingham,
      and we lost ourselves in memories.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000026
    m_Localized: "Once the guests had grown tired of conversation, Sir Blackmore
      gave a brief, rather empty speech on the virtues of patrons. Then it was Foxicia\u2019s
      turn: a stately polonaise, followed by a couple of her usual nocturnes \u2014
      the audience applauded."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000027
    m_Localized: 'Foxicia was surrounded by guests while I succumbed to boredom.

      I
      had likely overindulged in drink and failed to notice when she slipped away.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000028
    m_Localized: I do not know how much time had passed, but at some point, Sir Blackmore
      suggested a walk in the winter garden and a cigar. My head throbbed from the
      drink I had taken. Fortunately, Blackmore spoke freely and demanded no reply.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000029
    m_Localized: "This horror is beyond words!\nThe haze of drink cleared when I
      saw her lying on the wet ground.\nHer dress was soiled, her fur matted, and
      her eyes motionless.\nHow\u2026 how am I to live with this now!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000030
    m_Localized: 
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000031
    m_Localized: "Dr. Nicholas Purrley and Madame Foxicia are riding in a carriage
      to the estate of Sir Oswald Blackmore \u2014 the wealthiest badger in the kingdom."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000032
    m_Localized: A grand reception at the estate. Doctor Purrley meets his old acquaintance,
      Lady Bella Nottingham. The guests are introduced to a young romantic poet,
      Theodore Pawwood.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000033
    m_Localized: "Madame Foxicia plays a solemn polonaise and a couple of familiar
      nocturnes \u2014 the audience is enchanted."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000034
    m_Localized: Dr. Purrley retreats into solitude and alcoholic drink, while Madame
      Foxicia withdraws from the hall.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000035
    m_Localized: Dr. Purrley and Sir Blackmore stroll through the winter garden.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000036
    m_Localized: All the guests stand over the body of the deceased Madame Foxicia
      in the winter garden.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000037
    m_Localized: Focus on the items they're holding
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000038
    m_Localized: The scene contains a murder weapon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000039
    m_Localized: Focus on the wall
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000040
    m_Localized: Something is missing in this scene.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000041
    m_Localized: "Demonstrating a character\u2019s innocence"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000042
    m_Localized: "The characters\u2019 appearances have changed"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000043
    m_Localized: read the spread
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
